    <abstract id="aspace_fba20b25174a0773bf6f77fe238fef05">Papers and photographs documenting the Iselin family of New York, particularly the immediate descendants of banker Columbus O'Donnell Iselin (1851–1933) and his wife, Edith Colford (Jones) Iselin (1854–1930), as well as their Jones and O'Donnell forbears.</abstract>
    <physloc id="aspace_3cf7306cfcc6558744f07a93210250cd">Except for one oversize folder, all of this collection is stored offsite. To arrange to consult it, please go to <extref xlink:actuate="onRequest" xlink:href="https://www.nyhistory.org/library/visit">www.nyhistory.org/library/visit</extref>.</physloc>
    <langmaterial id="aspace_7112d6254e30a6b50633dc1531035d13">The majority of the documents in this collection are in English, with some instances of French, German, and Latin.</langmaterial>
