  <bioghist id="aspace_14155de4ff845c51df24c3580b3c8345">
    <head>Biographical note</head>
<p>Coal and iron investor ADRIAN GEORG ISELIN (1818–1905) and his wife, Eleanora O'Donnell (1821–1897) had at least seven children, among them sons ADRIAN GEORGE ISELIN JR. (1846–1935) and banker COLUMBUS O'DONNELL ISELIN (1851–1933). Columbus married EDITH COLFORD JONES (1854–1930), the daughter of Lewis Colford Jones and CATHERINE MARGARETTA BERRYMAN (c. 1829–1910). Among the children of Columbus and Edith Iselin were two sons, LEWIS ISELIN (1879–1928) and O'DONNELL ISELIN (1884–1971), and one daughter, ADRIENNE MARGARETTA ISELIN (1895–1967). Lewis Iselin married MARIE EMILIE DE NEUFVILLE (1883–1979), and together they had three children: COLUMBUS O'DONNELL ISELIN II (1904–1971), MARIE (ISELIN) LA FARGE (1907–1979), and LEWIS ISELIN JR. (1913–1990), who married SARAH CARY CURTIS (1915–1998). O'Donnell Iselin married MARGARET URLING SIBLEY (1893–1951). During World War I he served as railroad specialist on the staff of General John J. Pershing. Adrienne Iselin married Dudley Pierrepont Henry Gilbert (1898–1982), son of prominent "mansion architect" C. P. H. Gilbert (1861–1952). [Names in CAPITAL LETTERS are represented by documents and/or photographs in the collection.]</p>  </bioghist>
